7,Orang Kanaq Language: Critically Endangered Tongue of Johor Indigenous People - Native Tribe Info,https://nativetribe.info/orang-kanaq-language-critically-endangered-tongue-of-johor-indigenous-people/,"April 3, 2025 - The Orang Kanaq, also known as the Orang Seletar, are an indigenous group inhabiting the coastal regions of Johor, Malaysia. Their language, Orang Kanaq, is a Malayo-Polynesian language belonging to the Austronesian language family.",Orang Kanaq,Austronesian
8,About: Orang Kanaq language,https://dbpedia.org/page/Orang_Kanaq_language,"Orang Kanaq language is one of the Aboriginal Malay languages, grouped under the Austronesian language family. It is spoken by the Orang Kanaq, one of the 19 Orang Asli groups in Peninsular Malaysia. A variant of Malay, Orang Kanaq is distinct from the dialects spoken by ethnic Malays living ...",Orang Kanaq,Austronesian
